To connect a **DHT11 sensor module** to an **Arduino Uno R3**, follow these simple steps:

---

### ✅ **Required Components**
- Arduino Uno R3
- DHT11 sensor module (usually includes the sensor + a pull-up resistor)
- 4 jumper wires (male-to-male)
- Arduino IDE (software)

---

### 🔌 **Wiring Diagram**

| DHT11 Pin | Arduino Pin |
|-----------|-------------|
| VCC       | 5V          |
| GND       | GND         |
| DATA      | Pin 2       |
| (Not used)| (Left open) |

> 🔍 **Note**: Some DHT11 modules have a built-in pull-up resistor. If yours doesn’t, you can add a 10kΩ resistor between the DATA and VCC pins on the DHT11 module.

---

### 🧑‍💻 **Arduino Code Example**

```cpp
#include "DHT.h"

#define DHTPIN 2     // Digital pin connected to the DHT sensor
#define DHTTYPE DHT11   // DHT 11

DHT dht(DHTPIN, DHTTYPE);

void setup() {
  Serial.begin(9600);
  dht.begin();
}

void loop() {
  delay(2000); // Wait 2 seconds between readings

  float h = dht.readHumidity();
  float t = dht.readTemperature(); // Read temperature in Celsius

  if (isnan(h) || isnan(t)) {
    Serial.println("Failed to read from DHT sensor!");
    return;
  }

  Serial.print("Humidity: ");
  Serial.print(h);
  Serial.print(" %\t");
  Serial.print("Temperature: ");
  Serial.print(t);
  Serial.println(" *C");
}
