`ExceptionUtils.showStacktrace(...)` is a utility method that is part of the Apache Commons Lang library (`org.apache.commons.lang3.exception.ExceptionUtils`).  
It prints the complete stack-trace of a `Throwable` (or any of its subclasses) to the console (or to any `PrintStream`/`PrintWriter` you supply).

Quick example:

```java
import org.apache.commons.lang3.exception.ExceptionUtils;

public class Demo {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        try {
            riskyMethod();
        } catch (Exception ex) {
            // Print the full stack trace to System.err
            ExceptionUtils.printStackTrace(ex, System.err);
        }
    }

    private static void riskyMethod() {
        throw new RuntimeException("Boom!");
    }
}
```

